{"nodes": [{"id": "agent_review", "label": "Independent review: MiataBracing_review_v2.mp4 (agent_review.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_review_verdict", "label": "Verdict: not ready for voice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tower numbers match the xlsx, but conclusions lean on 0.2-0.5 mm gaps the data cannot rank, and a ninth unused PDF gives a different answer for the fender braces."}, {"id": "agent_review_b1_second_tower_measurement", "label": "B1: second tower measurement disagrees (+0.691 vs +0.237 mm)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same two scans, different measurement points; the 0.45 mm spread is as large as the gap between fender braces and strut tower brace, so 'fender braces did the most / 86 percent' is not safe until the owner says which measurement is right."}, {"id": "agent_review_distance_measurement_pdf", "label": "NB Miata Scan Fender Brace Jacked Engine Bay_Distance Measurement.pdf (948.382 -> 949.073)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_review_b2_ranking_and_mechanism_claims", "label": "B2: ranking and mechanism claims the data does not support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The script ranks at the end what it refused to rank earlier; 'diminishing returns' is a mechanism stated as fact while both braces (0.436) is worse than fender-only (0.237); no repeat scan shows the noise floor."}, {"id": "agent_review_b3_heat_map_claims", "label": "B3: whole-body heat-map claims asserted from maps showing panels and alignment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maps on a +-15 mm scale cannot see the 1.695 mm tower effect; twist is an interpretation that depends on the unknown alignment method; hinged panels and refitted fenders explain hot spots; colour reads are not values in the files."}, {"id": "agent_review_b4_wrong_burned_in_title", "label": "B4: wrong burned-in title in the fender-only section (5:09)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The fender IRL span ends on the first second of the fender+strut scanning shot, showing 'Scanning Fender Brace + Strut Brace' two sections early; fix by ending the span at rough cut ~321.1."}, {"id": "agent_review_b5_legend_card", "label": "B5: rough-cut 'How to read the heatmaps' legend card contradicts what follows", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its scale is +-8 mm while the next six heat cards are +-15, its ramp centres green on 0, and its text asserts things the pages do not show; replace with a card built from the real colour bar."}, {"id": "agent_review_b6_line_lengths", "label": "B6: line lengths assume 2.9 words/s, voice clone reads 2.2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At the clone's pace several IRL shots run out of picture and number lines are undercounted by dur(); time cards from the generated audio, not word count."}, {"id": "agent_review_non_blocking_issues", "label": "Non-blocking issues (picture vs words, cards)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_review_burned_in_titles_over_irl", "label": "Burned-in rough-cut titles over IRL footage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Violates the house rule 'never put text over IRL footage'; ask the team for clean exports or the owner's OK."}, {"id": "agent_review_terminology", "label": "Terminology: 'control' vs 'no bracing' instead of 'stock'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Stock' is used for both the car on the ground and the unbraced jacked state; one term per state avoids confusion."}, {"id": "agent_review_voice_analysis", "label": "Voice analysis vs owner transcript (So/actually/just tics, missing questions)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "13 of 27 lines open with 'So' and the owner's rhetorical questions are missing, so the draft does not sound like the owner."}, {"id": "agent_review_house_rules_to_confirm", "label": "House rules to confirm (voice clone consent, imperial units)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L85", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_review_line_by_line_rewrites", "label": "Line-by-line narration rewrites", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L89", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Numbers unchanged; IRL lines sized for 2.5 words/s or less; claims scoped to 'on this test'."}, {"id": "agent_review_cgi_and_graphics_plan", "label": "CGI and graphics plan (review proposal, 10 items)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All scans decimated and put in ONE frame (control prepped, rest with --like) or deviations are meaningless; on-screen numbers only from the xlsx/PDFs."}, {"id": "agent_review_heat_map_gate", "label": "Heat-map gate: reproduce the unbraced report pattern within ~2 mm first", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L132", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Our own best-fit alignment may not reproduce the reports' colours; if the gate fails, stay with cleaned PDF crops."}, {"id": "agent_review_open_questions_for_the_owner", "label": "Open questions for the owner", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L142", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_review_sign_off_pass_on_v3", "label": "Sign-off pass on v3 (not approved yet)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L154", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five wording changes required, then approved for owner review with no further pass."}, {"id": "agent_review_strut_top_cross_check_undercuts", "label": "v3 problem: strut-top cross-check undercuts unqualified conclusion lines", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L171", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "By the strut-top measure the fender braces did not reduce the spread and the unbraced spread is ~0.4 mm, so 'every setup cut that spread by more than half' holds only for the xlsx engine-bay width."}, {"id": "agent_review_body_percentages_disclosure", "label": "Body percentages (58/60/91/74) must be disclosed as our own calculation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": "L175", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They are computed from the STLs, not values in the xlsx or PDFs, so the script header claiming every number is from the files became false."}], "edges": [{"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_verdict", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_b1_second_tower_measurement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_b2_ranking_and_mechanism_claims", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_b3_heat_map_claims", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_b4_wrong_burned_in_title", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agent_review", "target": "agent_review_b5_legend_card", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "agent_review.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "age